# LOCAL EXPERIMENT FILE -- DO NOT COMMIT.
#
# Per-TU build flags for the flux kernel occupancy work.
# See Planning/CHECKPOINT.md and Planning/launch-bounds-plan.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Resource-usage remarks. Always want this on while experimenting.
#    Demangle with c++filt; the production kernel is
#      CalcFluxAll<Lb1E, Lb0E, eos_3p_idealgas>  =  <uct=true, pplim=false>
#
#    Remarks are emitted during compilation, before linking -- safe to Ctrl-C
#    once they scroll past. Getting output at all proves fluxes.cxx recompiled.
#      rm -f $CACTUS/configs/$CONFIG/build/AsterX/fluxes.cxx.o
#      gmake $CONFIG 2>&1 | tee ~/probe.log
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
fluxes.cxx.o: CXXFLAGS += -Rpass-analysis=kernel-resource-usage

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. COMPILE-TIME ACCELERATOR. Cuts the CalcFluxAll instantiation matrix from
#    16 (2 uct x 2 pplim x 4 EOS objects) to 2: idealgas, pplim=0, BOTH CT
#    schemes. ~8x less template work per rebuild. Guard lives in fluxes.cxx and
#    is inert without this -D.
#
#    Both CT schemes are kept on purpose: production is use_uct=yes, but the
#    large-grid TOV Z4c timing run is flux-CT (use_uct=no), and both timing runs
#    are idealgas + use_pplim=no. So this build IS usable for the timing runs --
#    only the test suite and the pplim / hybrid / tabulated configs need a full
#    rebuild.
#
#    The resulting binary ABORTS at runtime on use_pplim=yes, hybrid EOS, or
#    tabulated EOS. NEVER run the test suite or a golden check against it --
#    REMOVE this line and rebuild first.
#
#    ⚠ NOT codegen-neutral: cutting the matrix changes inlining of the shared
#    ReconX/EOS callees, so AGPR reads 32 here vs 40 in a full build. Rows from
#    a reduced build are comparable to each other ONLY; re-measure anything that
#    looks like a win in a full build before believing it.
fluxes.cxx.o: CXXFLAGS += -DASTERX_PROBE_IDEALGAS_ONLY

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. -mllvm flag sweep: REMOVED 2026-07-27, route exhausted on measurement.
#
#    All three mechanisms were run against the target <uct=1,pplim=0,idealgas>,
#    which needs AGPR 32 -> 0 to clear the 256-register cliff:
#      scheduling  --misched=gcn-max-occupancy   NULL  (it is already the
#                                                      AMDGPU default strategy)
#      allocation  --enable-deferred-spilling    AGPR 32->30, and CalcE uct1
#                                                SGPR spills 20/22/24->30/26/33
#      relaxed FP  -ffinite-math-only            AGPR 32->34 (worse)
#    Spread across three independent mechanisms: +-2 registers against a
#    32-register gap. Do not re-add PROBE_FLAGS or work down the remaining
#    Tier-2/3 candidate list -- they are variations on mechanisms already
#    measured at +-2. Two structural reasons it cannot work are recorded in
#    Planning/compiler-flags.md (the AGPRs are load-bearing live values, and a
#    TU-scoped flag cannot be aimed at CalcFluxAll because CalcE / CalcFstag /
#    CalcAux share this TU and demonstrably take collateral damage).
#
#    The occupancy route is now Planning/launch-bounds-plan.md: a per-launch-site
#    __launch_bounds__(256, 2) via a min_blocks template param on CarpetX
#    loop_box_device.
